title: Implementation of RFC-123
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Closes #64

    This PR implements approach 4 outlined in the issue and https://github.com/polkadot-fellows/RFCs/pull/123.

    Unresolved questions:
    - [x] Does the `CallContext::{Offchain, Onchain}` determine whether it's runtime calls / (block production or import)?
    - [x] dryRun RPC call will not work properly on the block setting the pending code, right? Is that a problem? A: No, transactions are getting invalidated any way by runtime upgrades because the spec version changes
    - [X] Do we want to pass `IgnorePendingCode` regardless in the higher level APIs? No
    - [x] Do we want to emit an event when pending code is set?
    - [x] Should the system_version check also be done on the node side (block production and import)?
    - [x] What is the best place to call `maybe_apply_pending_code_upgrade`?

    TODO:
    - [x] Fix failing tests
    - [x] New unit tests
    - [ ] e2e tests also for PVF upgrade
    - [x] make sure this https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/64#issuecomment-1691523876 is not a problem
